Maven is a build automation and project management tool.
It is mainly used for Java applications.
Maven manages project dependencies (libraries) automatically.
It uses a pom.xml file to configure the project.
pom.xml contains project details, dependencies, and build settings.
mvn compile compiles the source code.
mvn test runs automated tests.
mvn package creates a JAR or WAR file.
Maven follows a standard build lifecycle.
Maven helps developers build, test, package, and manage Java projects easily
